  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Speed. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Speed is a frantic two-player shedding card game where players race to get rid of all their cards onto two central piles. Play is simultaneous and real-time. Cards can be played if they are one rank higher or lower (e.g., 6 on 5, or 6 on 7) than the card on the pile. There are no turns. The first player to exhaust their hand and draw pile shouts 'Speed!' to win.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to play off all of your cards (hand and stock) onto the two center piles; the winner says Speed! to claim the win.',
    gameplay: 'Play is simultaneous with no turns. Players flip one face-down center card each to start. Each may play from hand onto either center pile when the card is one rank above, one below, or the same as the top of that pile; only one card at a time. Ace and two may be placed on each other (looping). When hand drops below five cards, draw from your stock to refill to five until stock is empty. When neither can play, both simultaneously flip one card from their side pile onto the center piles. When a player runs out of cards they say Speed! and win.',
    keyRules: [
      'Play one card at a time onto either center pile; rank must be one higher, one lower, or same as the top card.',
      'Refill hand from stock to five cards whenever hand has fewer than five.',
      'When stuck, both players flip one card from side pile onto center; if side piles empty, shuffle center stacks as new side piles.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two or more players.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card Anglo-American deck; the full pack is used and dealt between the two players (five to hand, 15 to stock each, and two center piles of six).',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card Anglo-American deck; the full pack is used and dealt between the two players (five to hand, 15 to stock each, and two center piles of six).',
      dealing: 'Each player is dealt five cards to form a hand and 15 cards face down to the side as a draw pile. Two six-card piles are then dealt in the center, face down.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Play is simultaneous with no turns. Players flip one face-down center card each to start. Each may play from hand onto either center pile when the card is one rank above, one below, or the same as the top of that pile; only one card at a time. Ace and two may be placed on each other (looping). When hand drops below five cards, draw from your stock to refill to five until stock is empty. When neither can play, both simultaneously flip one card from their side pile onto the center piles. When a player runs out of cards they say Speed! and win.',
